## Step 2: Homepage Snapshot

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet to implement the homepage snapshot features:

```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd

# Placeholder Data (replace with real data retrieval)
key_metrics = {
    "Total Bankroll": "£10,000",
    "Current Liability": "£500",
    "Exposure": "£300",
    "Daily P/L": "£150",
    "Open Trades": 5
}

recent_trades = pd.DataFrame({
    "Time": ["10:15", "10:45", "11:00", "11:30", "12:00"],
    "Bot": ["Bot A", "Bot B", "Bot C", "Bot A", "Bot D"],
    "Horse": ["Lightning", "Thunder", "Storm", "Rain", "Sunshine"],
    "Profit/Loss (£)": [25, -15, 35, 50, -20]
})

critical_alerts = [
    "⚠️ API Latency High",
    "✅ System Operational",
    "⚠️ High Liability on Bot B"
]

# Display Key Metrics
st.title("📈 Dashboard Homepage")
st.subheader("Key Metrics")
cols = st.columns(len(key_metrics))
for i, (metric, value) in enumerate(key_metrics.items()):
    cols[i].metric(label=metric, value=value)

# Recent Trades
st.subheader("Recent Trades")
st.dataframe(recent_trades, use_container_width=True)

# Critical Alerts
st.subheader("Critical Alerts")
for alert in critical_alerts:
    if "⚠️" in alert:
        st.warning(alert)
    elif "✅" in alert:
        st.success(alert)
```

